cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this survey, its data or its website, please cite it with the metadata below.
  It is a working draft: it has no DOI and has not been peer-reviewed.
title: "Jev and Typed Decision Models: An Empirical Survey of Calibration, Selective Control, and Open Implementations"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: "Luo"
    given-names: "Meng"
    website: "https://eurekaleo.github.io/"
version: 0.3.0
date-released: "2026-10-07"
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Eurekaleo/awesome-jev-survey"
url: "https://eurekaleo.github.io/awesome-jev-survey/"
abstract: >-
  An evidence survey of TypeSafe's Jev and Jev-like typed decision models: what their probabilities mean,
  when software should act on them, where typed decisions fail, and what open implementations release.
  It combines claim-level evidence records with source locators, ten cross-cutting findings, an audit of
  open models, benchmarks, applications and tools, a searchable website and a manuscript draft.
  Values are as reported by their sources.
keywords:
  - typed decision models
  - Jev
  - calibration
  - selective prediction
  - evidence audit
  - open models
  - survey
